6719:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_rcc_ex.c ****       (#) Enable CRS clock in IP MSP init which will use CRS functions
6720:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_rcc_ex.c **** 
6721:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_rcc_ex.c ****       (#) Call CRS functions as follows:
6722:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_rcc_ex.c ****           (##) Prepare synchronization configuration necessary for HSI48 calibration
6723:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_rcc_ex.c ****               (+++) Default values can be set for frequency Error Measurement (reload and error lim
6724:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_rcc_ex.c ****                         and also HSI48 oscillator smooth trimming.
6725:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_rcc_ex.c ****               (+++) Macro __HAL_RCC_CRS_RELOADVALUE_CALCULATE can be also used to calculate
6726:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_rcc_ex.c ****                         directly reload value with target and synchronization frequencies values
6727:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_rcc_ex.c ****           (##) Call function HAL_RCCEx_CRSConfig which
6728:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_rcc_ex.c ****               (+++) Resets CRS registers to their default values.
6729:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_rcc_ex.c ****               (+++) Configures CRS registers with synchronization configuration
6730:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_rcc_ex.c ****               (+++) Enables automatic calibration and frequency error counter feature
6731:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_rcc_ex.c ****            Note: When using USB LPM (Link Power Management) and the device is in Sleep mode, the
6732:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_rcc_ex.c ****            periodic USB SOF will not be generated by the host. No SYNC signal will therefore be
6733:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_rcc_ex.c ****            provided to the CRS to calibrate the HSI48 on the run. To guarantee the required clock
6734:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_rcc_ex.c ****            precision after waking up from Sleep mode, the LSE or reference clock on the GPIOs
6735:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_rcc_ex.c ****            should be used as SYNC signal.
6736:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_rcc_ex.c **** 
6737:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_rcc_ex.c ****           (##) A polling function is provided to wait for complete synchronization
6738:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_rcc_ex.c ****               (+++) Call function HAL_RCCEx_CRSWaitSynchronization()
6739:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_rcc_ex.c ****               (+++) According to CRS status, user can decide to adjust again the calibration or con
6740:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_rcc_ex.c ****                         application if synchronization is OK
