6742:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_rcc_ex.c ****       (#) User can retrieve information related to synchronization in calling function
6743:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_rcc_ex.c ****             HAL_RCCEx_CRSGetSynchronizationInfo()
6744:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_rcc_ex.c **** 
6745:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_rcc_ex.c ****       (#) Regarding synchronization status and synchronization information, user can try a new cali
6746:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_rcc_ex.c ****            in changing synchronization configuration and call again HAL_RCCEx_CRSConfig.
6747:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_rcc_ex.c ****            Note: When the SYNC event is detected during the downcounting phase (before reaching the
6748:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_rcc_ex.c ****            it means that the actual frequency is lower than the target (and so, that the TRIM value
6749:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_rcc_ex.c ****            incremented), while when it is detected during the upcounting phase it means that the ac
6750:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_rcc_ex.c ****            is higher (and that the TRIM value should be decremented).
6751:Drivers/STM32H5xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32h5xx_hal_rcc_ex.c **** 
